From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:14:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] msscript.ocx: connection points with the Error event, OLE
 control interfaces, persistence

The ScriptControl's connection points keep their sinks (Advise, Unadvise,
EnumConnections, EnumConnectionPoints). A script error raises the Error event
(AddCode, Eval, ExecuteStatement, Run); a handler that clears the Error object
makes the call succeed. IOleObject answers as a control that is invisible at
run time (host names, verbs, advise holder, extent, user type and class),
IPersistStreamInit saves and loads Timeout, AllowUI and UseSafeSubset with dirty
tracking, IQuickActivate connects the container's sinks, IViewObjectEx answers
extents and hit tests, IOleControl freezes events, IPointerInactive and the script
site answer their remaining calls; _AboutBox shows an about box.

